      "text_unit_id": "tu_0001",
      "verbatim_text": "Dual-chamber cardiac pacing is indicated to reduce recurrent syncope in patients aged >40 years, with severe, unpredictable, recurrent syncope who have: • spontaneous documented symptomatic asystolic pause(s) >3 s or asymptomatic pause(s) >6 s due to sinus arrest or AVB; or • cardioinhibitory carotid sinus syndrome; or • asystolic syncope during tilt testing.62,219,220,226,228,229"
